BT /F2 15.00 Tf 80.00 560.00 Td (Important distinction) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 80.00 532.00 Td (A C++ class can be declared once and implemented in many compilation units.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 80.00 512.00 Td (That is what Rover does. The scattered files are not separate Rover classes; they are grouped method bodies.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 80.00 492.00 Td (For example, sensors.cpp defines Rover::update_compass\(\), Rover::update_wheel_encoder\(\), and Rover::read_rangefinders\(\).) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F2 15.00 Tf 80.00 438.00 Td (Why ArduPilot uses this layout) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 10.00 Tf 95.00 408.00 Td (- Rover is a large vehicle class with many responsibilities: initialization, radio input, sensors, navigation, output, failsafes, logging, and commands.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 10.00 Tf 95.00 384.00 Td (- Splitting method implementations by subsystem keeps each file reviewable without changing the object model.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 10.00 Tf 95.00 360.00 Td (- The scheduler table in Rover.cpp is the best high-level map of which methods run periodically.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 10.00 Tf 95.00 336.00 Td (- Mode classes are separate classes because each mode has its own behavior and overrides the shared Mode interface.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 10.00 Tf 95.00 312.00 Td (- Feature classes such as Sailboat, AP_Arming_Rover, and GCS_Rover are separate objects owned by Rover or ParametersG2.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F2 15.00 Tf 80.00 240.00 Td (Practical reading order) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 95.00 212.00 Td (1. Start at Rover/Rover.h to see owned state and declared methods.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 95.00 190.00 Td (2. Read Rover/Rover.cpp to understand scheduler timing and the main loop.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 95.00 168.00 Td (3. Follow the relevant subsystem file, such as sensors.cpp, radio.cpp, Steering.cpp, or failsafe.cpp.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 95.00 146.00 Td (4. For behavior differences by driving mode, read mode.h and the matching mode_*.cpp file.) Tj ET
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 95.00 124.00 Td (5. For parameters and owned library objects, read Parameters.h and Parameters.cpp.) Tj ET
